<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62579" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λέρνα</span></b> , ἡ,
			<u>Lerna</u>, a marsh in Argolis, the mythol. abode of the
		Hydra, <i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			<u>Cleom.</u>
			15
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Paus.
			2.4.5
		</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λέρνη</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Cratin.
			347
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			8.6.8
		</span></i>, etc.: gen. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λέρνης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					652
				</span></i>
			, etc.: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λέρνη κακῶν</span>
			an abyss of ills, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λ. θεατῶν</span>, of the
			theatre, Cratin.l.c.:—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λερναῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				314
			</span></i>, etc.; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				191
			</span></i> (lyr.):—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λερναία
			χολή</span>, of malignant anger, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Trag.Adesp.</u>
				229
			</span></i>.</div>
